# UCOS Ω∞ — machinery transients (UMB-IMP-001). The registration re-entrancy lock
# is created/removed by register.sh and must never be committed or seen as drift.
00-BOOK/tools/.register.lock
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# EC3 Phase-3 — runtime governance telemetry. The enforcement / synchronization /
# certification audit logs are per-clone OPERATIONAL runtime state (not repository
# artifacts). They live ONLY here, are written solely by
# 00-BOOK/tools/governance_telemetry.py, and must never be tracked or seen as
# drift. This is the permanent remediation for telemetry-induced non-determinism.
.runtime/


# EC-1 engine (EPIC-001 Foundation) build / test transients.
.ec1-venv/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml

# UCOS-GOV-006 (GOV-005 §5.1/§6.8) — formally declare generated evidence and
# editor/office lock files as NON-ARTIFACTS bounded by version control. Generated
# evidence is deterministically re-derivable output (regenerated each run), not a
# registerable repository artifact; ~$ files are transient Office owner/lock temp
# files. Declaring them here makes the intent explicit and keeps eligibility a
# pure function of the tracked/un-ignored corpus for all future growth.
determinism-evidence/
~$*


# EPIC-UKDA (Universal Knowledge & Decision Architecture) — generated canonical
# knowledge store + handbooks. The single authored-once source of this knowledge is
# engine/knowledge/seed.py (tracked engineering code); the knowledge/ directory is
# deterministically re-derivable output (`ucos-knowledge init` / `ucos-knowledge
# docs`), i.e. a GENERATED ARTIFACT (GOV-005 §5.3) bounded by the ignore authority,
# never hand-registered. Regenerated each run; must never be tracked or seen as drift.
# Anchored with a leading slash so ONLY the repo-root store is ignored — the
# engine/knowledge/ source package and its tests remain tracked.
/knowledge/


# UAKOS-CLOSURE-002 — deterministic engine OUTPUT (GOV-005 §5.3, re-derivable). The
# authored sources (closure_engine.py / phase2_engine.py / phase3_engine.py + README /
# CHARTER / CONSOLIDATION-PLAN / PHASE-002-README / PHASE-INTERFACE-CONTRACT) remain
# tracked; the numbered reports and JSON state are regenerated each run (`make closure`
# / `make closure-phase2` / `make closure-phase3`) and must never be tracked or seen as
# drift. Mirrors the existing determinism-evidence/ and /knowledge/ generated-artifact policy.
00-MASTER/UAKOS-CLOSURE-002/[0-9][0-9]-*.md
00-MASTER/UAKOS-CLOSURE-002/closure.json
00-MASTER/UAKOS-CLOSURE-002/phase2.json
00-MASTER/UAKOS-CLOSURE-002/phase3.json

# intelligence/die — RC-1 pre-sealing audit identified imports.py as an unverified
# orphan (no __init__.py, no importers, no tests, not packaged/covered). Excluded from
# the RC-1 baseline until it is wired + tested; ignored here so it is not sealed as
# verified implementation and does not surface as drift.
intelligence/die/


# GPR-001 S1 (GOV-005 §5.3 / §5.1; closes GPA-001 G1/G3) — 00-MASTER program-lane
# EXECUTION EVIDENCE and ENGINE JSON STATE are deterministically re-derivable engine
# OUTPUT (per-run register/validate/certify/determinism logs + provenance / gap-graph
# state), regenerated each run by their phase engines, never hand-registered. Declared
# NON-ARTIFACTS bounded by the ignore authority — mirrors the determinism-evidence/,
# /knowledge/, and UAKOS-CLOSURE-002 generated-artifact policy. Scoped to the 00-MASTER
# program lane ONLY: the tracked data/_evidence/ canonical certification artifacts
# (UCOS-DATA-*) are a distinct, registered family and are deliberately NOT matched here.
00-MASTER/**/evidence/
00-MASTER/UAKOS-PHASE-001B/provenance.json
00-MASTER/UAKOS-PHASE-004/10-UNIVERSAL-GAP-DEPENDENCY-GRAPH.json



# URI-000001 (Universal Realization Intelligence) — generated realization artifacts and
# the consolidated evidence bundle. Both are deterministically re-derivable OUTPUT
# (GOV-005 §5.3): the authored source is intelligence/realization/** (tracked engineering
# code) plus the canonical knowledge store it reads; `python -m intelligence.realization
# realize` regenerates every byte. Declared NON-ARTIFACTS bounded by the ignore authority
# so they are never hand-registered and never surface as drift — mirrors the existing
# /knowledge/, determinism-evidence/ and UAKOS-CLOSURE-002 generated-artifact policy.
# Anchored with a leading slash so ONLY the repo-root generated tree is ignored; the
# intelligence/realization/ source package and its tests remain tracked.
/realization/
data/_evidence/URI-000001/


# UCOS-URI-001 / UCOS-UPI-001 (Universal Research + Publication Intelligence) —
# generated research corpus and generated publication set. Both are deterministically
# re-derivable OUTPUT (GOV-005 §5.3): the authored sources are intelligence/research/**
# and intelligence/publication/** (tracked engineering code) plus the canonical knowledge
# store they read; `make research` / `make publication` regenerate every byte and both
# engines self-prove determinism (`research verify` / `publication verify`). Every
# publication additionally carries the provenance banner "GENERATED FROM CANONICAL
# KNOWLEDGE BY UCOS-UPI-001 — DO NOT EDIT BY HAND". Declared NON-ARTIFACTS bounded by the
# ignore authority so they never consume permanent corpus identities and never surface as
# drift — mirrors the existing /knowledge/, /realization/, determinism-evidence/ and
# UAKOS-CLOSURE-002 generated-artifact policy. The one AUTHORED file the publication engine
# reads from inside its own output tree (the optional format-extension descriptor) is
# explicitly re-admitted so a future authored format remains a registerable artifact.
intelligence/UCOS-URI-001/
intelligence/UCOS-UPI-001/
!intelligence/UCOS-UPI-001/publication-formats.json



# UCOS-RFP-001 W2-00 P-01 (RFP-1 / CLO-01 / CLO-05) — git bundle archives. A bundle is a
# version-control TRANSPORT container: a serialization of the object database, produced by
# `git bundle create` for backup or offline transfer. It is an environment output, so
# RFP-001's class_derivation places it in CLS-TRANSIENT at the first ordered question
# ("Is it absent from version control? → CLS-TRANSIENT if environment output"), and
# CLS-TRANSIENT is EXEMPT from the fixed point by construction — never tracked, therefore
# outside it. Left un-ignored, a bundle written into the working tree is an untracked entry
# that no exclusion authority accounts for, so it counts against CLO-01
# (initial_dirty_entries) and CLO-05 (untracked_outside_excluded) and aborts `make rfp-gate`
# before any pipeline stage executes — and it is separately retained by UCOS-RIB-001's
# scoped observation, failing GATE-12 (Repository Clean). Measured consequence of its
# absence: a 92,678,041-byte bundle at the repository root held G-15 CLOSED at
# df763bf while every producer in the declared pipeline was in fact convergent.
# Declared at the GENUS (*.bundle) rather than by filename so recurrence is structurally
# impossible for any future bundle under any name — mirrors the existing
# determinism-evidence/, /knowledge/ and /realization/ generated-artifact policy.
# Bundles belong in durable storage OUTSIDE the repository, never inside the tree they back up.
*.bundle
